SetEconomicsTest
├── when economics is address zero
│   └── it should revert with {InvalidEconomics}
└── when economics is not address zero
    ├── when economics rollup differs from the rollup
    │   └── it should revert with {InvalidEconomicsRollup}
    └── when economics rollup matches the rollup
        ├── when economics fee asset differs from the rollup fee asset
        │   └── it should revert with {InvalidEconomicsFeeAsset}
        └── when economics fee asset matches the rollup fee asset
            ├── when economics genesis time differs from the rollup genesis time
            │   └── it should revert with {InvalidEconomicsGenesisTime}
            └── when economics genesis time matches the rollup genesis time
                ├── when economics slot duration differs from the rollup slot duration
                │   └── it should revert with {InvalidEconomicsSlotDuration}
                └── when economics slot duration matches the rollup slot duration
                    ├── when economics epoch duration differs from the rollup epoch duration
                    │   └── it should revert with {InvalidEconomicsEpochDuration}
                    └── when economics epoch duration matches the rollup epoch duration
                        ├── when economics proof submission epochs differ from the rollup
                        │   └── it should revert with {InvalidEconomicsProofSubmissionEpochs}
                        └── when economics proof submission epochs match the rollup
                            ├── when scheduling a valid replacement
                            │   └── it should schedule the replacement for the next epoch
                            ├── when the pending chain is still unproven
                            │   └── it should still schedule the replacement
                            └── when called multiple times for the same activation epoch
                                └── it should let the last call win
